p=root/'docs/DECISIONS.md';s=p.read_text();s+='''\n\n## Continue with routed switched-cap packet; recalibrate at each state range — 2026-10-13\n\nThe center-state packet method remains the selected next implementation because the compact parent now passes DRC/LVS/GDS readback and delivers matched signed8mV-class updates with less than0.05mV drift over5ms. Use parent v12 while calibrating; the center packet steps must not be reused at endpoints without measurement. The endpoint transient shows beta/handoff errors up to13.9mV and wrong/small updates for some old packet settings. Continue with state-conditioned beta/baseline and positive/negative packet transfer calibration, then exercise the original-float recurrence. This is a provisional article implementation, not an acceptance claim. The first long-bus parent is rejected functionally because routed control coupling dominated the update; compact reroutes remain experiments until extracted simulation passes.\n\nEvidence: `artifacts/analog_asic/layout/gf180_sc_state_packet_compact_v12/qualification.json`, center and endpoint reports cited in RESULTS.md.\n''';p.write_text(s)
# ARCHITECTURE.
p=root/'docs/ARCHITECTURE.md';s=p.read_text();s+='''\n\n## Routed switched-capacitor membrane packet — 2026-10-13\n\nThe active charge-delivery candidate uses one shared MIM packet per update channel: sample/park the packet against membrane state, disconnect the sample path, drive the bottom plate from an analog weight-dependent source, then release the packet while the membrane stores the resulting charge. Weight determines the signed charge amplitude; it does not change presynaptic firing frequency. The current v12 physical parent integrates the state storage, packet capacitor, and park/sample/drive TGs. It exposes one-source controls directly at their child pins and routes only shared nets across the parent. Control routing matters physically: an earlier blanket-bus parent had extracted control-to-state coupling above12fF and caused roughly170mV sample-edge disturbance.\n\nUse the nominal v12 center transfer as a calibration point only. At TT27 with externally supplied phase timing and voltage maps,94mV/45mV packet steps produce+8.01/-8.10mV and hold within0.04mV over5ms. Low/high state response, beta mapping, analog weight source, physical timing, saturation detector, full PLIF recurrence, and full-chip service remain open. Keep original float parameters; no QAT or quantized membrane path defines analog precision.\n''';p.write_text(s)
# PROGRESS.
